{
  "agent": "holmes-mcp",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n- In the `billing-api` pod logs, repeated `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)` errors occur alongside rising memory warnings.\n- In deployment `billing-api` (namespace `demo-apps`), `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` is configured to `900`.\n- In DBProxy `billing-db-proxy` (namespace `ack-system`), `spec.idleClientTimeout` is set to `600` seconds.\n\n### Ruled-Out Leads\n- Application memory leak ruled out because memory growth is a byproduct of unreleased dead connection slots per RB-014 and INC-2024-0312.\n- ALB timeout mismatch ruled out because deployment CI-2455 raised LB and HTTP keep-alive timeouts, leaving DB pool connections as the failing path.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe DBProxy `idleClientTimeout` (600s) is shorter than `billing-api`'s connection pool idle timeout (900s), causing the proxy to close idle database connections prematurely (RB-014).\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe platform/infrastructure team should remove or raise `idleClientTimeout` on DBProxy `billing-db-proxy` above 900s, or the billing team should lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`.",
